<template>
	<DocsPage
		product="Meeko i18n"
		locale="en"
		title="Playground"
		description="Try translations, plurals, selectors, formats and RTL direction with the real module."
	>
		<TranslationLab />
		<h2 id="how-it-works">One contract in three languages</h2>
		<p>
			The playground uses Spanish, English and Arabic JSON catalogs registered in
			<code>meeko.config.ts</code>. Signals update the arguments of
			<code>t</code>; the language links point to
			<code>switchLocalePath</code>
			and load the other language in a full navigation, keeping the search and the fragment of the URL.
		</p>
		<p>
			This page is a project file at
			<code>app/pages/en/playground.meeko</code>: it replaces the
			<code>/en/playground</code>
			route that the module generates from
			<code>app/pages/playground.meeko</code>, so its prose can be written in English. Every page of this site has its English file in
			<code>app/pages/en/</code>; a page without one would show the Spanish original with an «untranslated» notice.
		</p>
		<p>
			Its links are written once:
			<MeekoLink to="/routing">languages and routes</MeekoLink>
			points to
			<code>/en/routing</code>
			here and to
			<code>/routing</code>
			in Spanish, and
			<MeekoLink
				to="/routing"
				hreflang="es"
			>
				the Spanish version
			</MeekoLink>
			forces another language with
			<code>hreflang</code>.
		</p>
	</DocsPage>
</template>
